KG42.register("source_edge_archive-cace09428aae0be1d8b56fc1",{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E003","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E003","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-E-26"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C003"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","target":"COMP-20e312b579d3a493","source_occurrence_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. | Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. | Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. | Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. | Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. | Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. | Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. | Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"73150e2b268da0d7fbdd287072e3b6627fe73cd93dad0bb45ce4d897c867980d","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Information, allocation, governance or payment coordination in this mechanism: ESP computes internal buying/selling prices from supply-demand ratio and grid tariffs; prosumers iteratively reschedule; preserve service-fee and balance conditions.","target_definition":"Internal prices are tariff-bounded functions of the zone supply-demand ratio, with distinct buying/selling roles for net power signs. For SDR above one both equal the export tariff; for SDR between zero and one retain the source nonlinear selling-price formula and buying-price cost/balance construction. Do not generalize denominator limits or fee accounting beyond source conditions.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The ESP recalculates the internal prices. Scope: Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-E-26"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3571 In order to facilitate the organization of energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. | Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. | Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. | Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. | Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. | Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. | Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. | Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E003","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-E-26"]},"paper_scope_note":"Retain the positive and negative net-power branches, ESP organizational responsibilities, cost valuation, and the shared service fee sub-item; the iterative price, final price, and grid trading after failure cannot be treated as identical."}});
